# Performance Rules

## Storage

❌ BAD - AsyncStorage (slow, async):
import AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage';
await AsyncStorage.setItem('token', token);
const token = await AsyncStorage.getItem('token');

✅ GOOD - MMKV (30x faster, sync):
import { storage } from '@/services/storage';
storage.set('token', token);
const token = storage.getString('token');

## Zustand Selectors

❌ BAD - subscribes to entire store, re-renders on any change:
const { user, settings, notifications } = useAuthStore();
// Component re-renders when ANY of these change

✅ GOOD - subscribe only to what you need:
const user = useAuthStore(s => s.user);
// Only re-renders when user changes

## Lists

❌ BAD - FlatList without optimization:
<FlatList
  data={items}
  renderItem={({ item }) => <Item data={item} />}
/>

✅ GOOD - FlashList with memoized items:
const MemoizedItem = memo(Item);
<FlashList
  data={items}
  renderItem={({ item }) => <MemoizedItem data={item} />}
  estimatedItemSize={80}
/>

## Re-renders

❌ BAD - object/array created every render:
<UserCard user={{ name, avatar }} />
<List items={items.filter(i => i.active)} />

✅ GOOD - memoize objects and derived data:
const userData = useMemo(() => ({ name, avatar }), [name, avatar]);
const activeItems = useMemo(() => items.filter(i => i.active), [items]);
